<h1>Build extension dialing and a line test with VoiceML.</h1>
<p class="lede">A fictional defense computer answers the phone. Pressing 1 calls another company&rsquo;s switchboard and keys an extension automatically once it answers, so the caller never navigates someone else&rsquo;s menu. Pressing 2 starts a line test that plays the caller&rsquo;s own voice back to them. It is one document published on voiceml.org, with no application server.</p>
<p class="hero-actions">
	<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/signup/">Free trial</a>
	<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="{{ site.voicemlReferenceUrl }}/nouns/number/">&lt;Number&gt; reference</a>
</p>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>What callers get</h2>
	<ul class="features-grid">
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "hash" %}</span>
			<h3>An extension, dialed for them</h3>
			<p><code>sendDigits</code> waits for the other system to answer, pauses, and keys the extension, so callers reach a person behind someone else&rsquo;s menu with one key.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "activity" %}</span>
			<h3>A line test</h3>
			<p><code>&lt;Echo&gt;</code> plays everything the caller says back to them, to check for delay, echo, or poor audio on their line.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "broadcast-pin" %}</span>
			<h3>A touch tone as a cue</h3>
			<p><code>&lt;Play digits&gt;</code> plays a touch tone to mark the start of the test, with no audio file needed.</p>
		</li>
	</ul>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Before you start</h2>
	<ol>
		<li><strong>A VoiceML account with a phone number.</strong> See <a href="/voiceml/">VoiceML</a> or <a href="/signup/">start a free trial</a>.</li>
		<li><strong>The number of the phone system to dial into</strong>, the extension, and how long its greeting runs before it accepts keys.</li>
	</ol>
	<div class="alert alert-warning" role="note">
		<p><strong>The switchboard number and extension in this document are fictional.</strong> The number uses the 555-0100 to 555-0199 range, which is set aside for fiction. Replace both before you publish.</p>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Step 1: Publish the document and point the number at it</h2>
	<p>Replace the switchboard number and the extension in <code>sendDigits</code>, then publish it at <a href="{{ site.voicemlPublisherUrl }}">voiceml.org</a> and set the <code>/r/</code> URL it returns as the phone number&rsquo;s voice URL. Keep the URL exactly as returned, <code>key</code> included, and don&rsquo;t post it publicly.</p>
	<p class="code-block-header">main.xml</p>
	<pre class="code-block" data-lang="xml"><code>{{ voicemlSamples["wopr-line"].main | escape }}</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Step 2: Test it</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>Call the number and press 2. After the tone, speak; you hear yourself a moment later. Hang up to end the test.</li>
		<li>Call again and press 1. Listen as the switchboard answers and the extension is keyed for you.</li>
	</ol>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>How it works</h2>
	<div class="table-container">
		<table class="data-table">
			<caption>The markup behind each feature</caption>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th scope="col">Markup</th>
					<th scope="col">What it does</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>&lt;Number sendDigits="wwww1983#"&gt;</code></td><td>After the dialed number answers, waits two seconds (each <code>w</code> is half a second, each <code>W</code> a full second), then sends the keys 1, 9, 8, 3, and <kbd>#</kbd> on that call.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>&lt;Play digits="#"/&gt;</code></td><td>Plays the <kbd>#</kbd> touch tone to the caller, a beep with no audio file to host.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>&lt;Echo/&gt;</code></td><td>Plays the caller&rsquo;s own audio back to them until they hang up. Nothing after it runs, so it comes last.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<p>Tune the pause in <code>sendDigits</code> to the system you call: if the keys arrive while its greeting is still playing, it may ignore them. Add a <code>w</code> for every half second more it needs.</p>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Where the movie turns up</h2>
	<div class="table-container">
